+## Follow-up: separate conclusion and explicit implementation
+
+This feedback supersedes earlier closing-string and `submit_explore` contracts.
+Rename that tool to `submit_question`, which always posts a next question. Add a
+separate `submit_conclusion` with `summary`, `to_be_implemented`, and `future_work`
+string arguments plus turn identity and final-answer interpretation. Preserve the
+same attribution, validation, session binding and idempotent retry rules.
+
+Conclusions open their own page, like Opening, and remain reachable through history
+controls. Do not append a conclusion to the final question. Show summary and future
+work outside an editable task box populated only with `to_be_implemented`. An
+explicit Implement action sends only the edited tasks through the existing shared
+prompt delivery method. It authorizes implementation and validation of those tasks;
+submitting a conclusion alone does not. Preserve edits on failure, allow cancelling
+queued delivery, and distinguish request delivery from completed implementation.
